sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch03-08> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch03-08: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.54" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.543"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.57"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Plot databases can test the biogeographic pattern that some rare plants are locally numerous, and a few demographic models speak to Allee effects. Enemy-relative stock size, which is the mechanism, is usually missing. The result can support or weaken the pattern for plants and only proxy the survival rule." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Test for positive density dependence at low density in demographic models, and test whether geographically rare plants are locally abundant where they occur, relative to their enemies' density. Allee effects plus locally high density of range-restricted plants would support the statement; strictly negative density dependence and rare plants that are also locally sparse would count against it." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Local abundance of rare plants can reflect habitat specialization rather than swamping of enemies.", "Enemy density is rarely recorded in the same plots as the plant census.", "Most matrix models are not density-dependent, so Allee effects are a small, biased subset." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch03-08--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch03-08 by Grok 4.7: 0.58" ;
